---
title: Specimen Curation
sidebar:
  label: Overview
  order: 0
---

`Specimen curation` is a project tool for checking physical material against
its records after collecting. It writes curation fields to many records in one
pass, so you don't have to open each specimen form. The tool is in beta.

## Open the tool

Open a project and select `Curation` in the tool dock on the project
dashboard. The dock shows it by default. If you removed it, select
`Edit list` in the dock and turn `Curation` back on.

The mode selector at the top of the screen picks what you curate. Only one
mode is available for now:

- [Tissue curation](/en/usages/curation/tissue-curation/): scan specimen part
  tubes, and parasite tubes if you choose, into storage boxes. Each tube gets
  a museum code and the next free cell as its storage location.

## How curation changes records

Curation writes to the same fields you would edit in the specimen form. Tissue
curation writes `Museum permanent` or `Museum loan` and `Storage location` on
a part or parasite. The values show on the record, in the data table, and in
every export.

Each change is saved when it is made. The session log lists what this visit
changed, and `Undo` reverts the most recent change, including any value it
replaced. Closing the screen ends the session. Changes stay saved, but the
log and undo history are cleared.

Back up the database before curating a large collection. See
[Backup database](/en/usages/export/#backup-database).
